  "decision": "Reduced both estimates by one point, to 62% for $5K and 30% for $10K. The U.S. 10-year yield rose to 5.106%, its highest since 2007, the dollar strengthened, oil returned above $100, and markets priced a 66% chance of another October Fed hike. ETH fell about 4% to $2.67K and Ethereum recorded $231M of daily bridge outflows, reversing part of the prior breakout confirmation. The latest ETF session remained incomplete after two strong inflow days, while staking continued to rise and L1 revenue improved modestly. Cyclical liquidity therefore returns to the score floor, separately from the unchanged structural fiscal-debasement thesis. Direct L1 economics remain small relative to application fees, preserving the explicit $10K value-capture penalty. No catalyst crossed a color threshold and no thesis-breaking event occurred."
